From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: define an AC_NUM fallback in sr_cmd.h

sr_cmd.h reaches rtmp.h's include chain through mcu/andes_core.h, which runs
before rt_config.h includes dabs_qos.h, so AC_NUM is still undefined when
struct SR_STA_INFO_T declares u2AvgMPDULength[AC_NUM]. Add the same guarded
fallback dabs_qos.h, red.h and wapp_cmm_type.h already use.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/include/sr_cmd.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/sr_cmd.h
@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@
 /*******************************************************************************
  *    MACRO
  ******************************************************************************/
+/*
+ * sr_cmd.h is reached through rtmp.h -> mcu/andes_core.h, before rt_config.h
+ * gets to include dabs_qos.h, so AC_NUM is not defined yet.  Keep the same
+ * guarded fallback the other three headers use.
+ */
+#ifndef AC_NUM
+#define AC_NUM							4
+#endif
 
 /*******************************************************************************
  *    TYPES
